# What this repository can produce that must not be committed.
#
# Only skills/ ships; everything else here is maintainer material.
# Nothing in this repository is built or compiled, so there are no
# build outputs to ignore -- the entries below are local tooling,
# secrets, and editor or OS scratch.

# Agent harness config, and the three categories of agent skill that
# can appear under .claude/skills/.
#
# 1. Third-party skills installed for development (e.g. genesis) are
#    never committed. See docs/devs/design-process.md for what they
#    are and how to re-add them. They stay ignored because they do
#    not carry the dev- prefix.
# 2. Maintainer-only dev skills ARE committed. That is the one
#    exception below, and the dev- prefix is what grants it: a dev
#    skill misnamed without the prefix is silently ignored by git and
#    vanishes on the next clone. See
#    docs/devs/decisions/0014-dev-skills-outside-skills-dir.md.
# 3. This repo's shippable skills live in skills/ and are loaded with
#    `claude --plugin-dir .`, so no mirror of them belongs here.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/dev-*/
.agents/

# Secrets and local environment
*.env
.env
.env.*

# Python, for the PyYAML that tests/check-workflow-template.sh needs
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
.history/
*~

# OS scratch
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
